GTIG reports a zero-day exploit it believes was developed with AI that criminals planned to use in mass exploitation and that its disclosure may have prevented, not one confirmed in use in the wild; it needs valid credentials. CANFAIL and LONGSTREAM embed LLM-generated decoy code as obfuscation rather than calling an LLM at runtime, PROMPTSPY is the report's AI-driven malware, and UNC5673 pools LLM accounts; the report ties neither stolen LLM keys nor SANDCLOCK to a criminal market for AI access, and TeamPCP's entry points were compromised PyPI packages and malicious pull requests.
